Medical Sciences</collab></person-group><source>International Ethical Guidelines for Biomedical Research Involving Human Subjects Geneva</source><year>1993</year></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health and Human Services [DHHS]</collab></person-group><source>Title 45 Code of Federal Regulations Part 46 Protection of Human Subjects</source><year>1991</year><publisher-name>Bethesda. MD: National Institutes of Health, Office for Protection from Research Risks</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health</collab></person-group><source>Local Research Ethics Committees (HSG(91)5) London</source><year>1991</year></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holm</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Danish Research Ethics Committee System, Overview and Critical Assessment Research Involving Human Participants V2</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Online Ethics Center at the National Academy of Engineering</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.onlineethics.org/cms/8082.aspx"/></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oleskey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Pesticide Testing in Humans: Ethics and Public Policy</article-title><source>Environmental Health Perspectives</source><year>2004</year><volume>112</volume><fpage>914</fpage><lpage>919</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15175182</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Soskolne</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ethical, Social and L